From: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 01:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: AN7563 - bypass PPE in airoha_dev_open when no NPU

Root cause of the AN7563 "lan/eth0 rx_packets++ from FE counter but
driver never sees a packet, IRQ count = 0, AN7563 RX trace never
fires" symptom:

  airoha_dev_open() sets GDM_FWD_CFG so that frame-engine traffic on a
  GDM port is forwarded to FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1, expecting the PPE engine
  to lookup the FOE table and (on miss) forward the packet to the QDMA
  CPU DMA port.

  But airoha_ppe_hw_init() (which programs PPE TB_BASE, TB_HASH_CFG,
  TB_CFG and the per-port "default CPU port" rule) only runs from
  airoha_ppe_offload_setup() the first time a netfilter flow rule is
  added, and that path only fires once airoha_ppe_npu_get() returns a
  live NPU. EN7581 / AN7583 have an NPU firmware blob that brings the
  PPE engine online on boot. AN7563 has no NPU node in our DTS at all
  (we have not landed the GPL NPU image), so airoha_ppe_offload_setup()
  is never reached and PPE1 remains in reset state.

  In that state the FE happily delivers frames into PPE1 (the GDM RX
  hardware counters keep ticking, which is what eth0/statistics/
  rx_packets reads) but PPE1 silently drops them. They never reach
  QDMA, no airoha_irq_handler fires, no NAPI poll runs.

Fix: add a per-SoC "no_npu" quirk. When set, airoha_dev_open() picks
FE_PSE_PORT_CDM1 / CDM2 (the QDMA CPU DMA ports) directly instead of
FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1, so the FE-to-CPU path stays open even without a PPE
hw_init step. Set it on AN7563 only; EN7581 / AN7583 keep the original
PPE1 path so flow offload still works for them.

Also add a one-shot dev_info on each ndo_open so we can see in dmesg
which pse_port a given GDM netdev ended up wired to.

Verified by build only on this commit; runtime verification will land
in the next iteration once the test board boots the new image.

Signed-off-by: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -594,6 +594,16 @@ struct airoha_eth_soc_data {
 	 * so on AN7563 we can safely skip it.
 	 */
 	bool ppe_skip_flush_sram;
+	/*
+	 * AN7563 has no NPU node / NPU firmware bring-up, so
+	 * airoha_ppe_offload_setup() never runs and the PPE engine
+	 * stays in reset state. The default forwarding rule set by
+	 * airoha_dev_open() (pse_port = FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1) leaves
+	 * frame-engine packets stuck inside PPE1 instead of being
+	 * delivered to QDMA. On AN7563 bypass PPE and forward
+	 * directly to the QDMA CPU DMA port (CDM1/CDM2).
+	 */
+	bool no_npu;
 	struct {
 		int (*get_src_port_id)(struct airoha_gdm_port *port, int nbq);
 		u32 (*get_vip_port)(struct airoha_gdm_port *port, int nbq);
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1778,8 +1778,21 @@ static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_de
 	int err, len = ETH_HLEN + dev->mtu + ETH_FCS_LEN;
 	struct airoha_gdm_port *port = netdev_priv(dev);
 	struct airoha_qdma *qdma = port->qdma;
+	struct airoha_eth *eth = qdma->eth;
+	u8 qdma_id = qdma - &eth->qdma[0];
 	u32 pse_port = FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1;
 
+	/* AN7563 has no NPU bring-up: PPE never gets airoha_ppe_hw_init(),
+	 * so forwarding GDM packets through PPE1 silently drops them.
+	 * Bypass PPE and forward straight to QDMA CPU DMA port instead.
+	 */
+	if (eth->soc->no_npu)
+		pse_port = qdma_id ? FE_PSE_PORT_CDM2 : FE_PSE_PORT_CDM1;
+
+	dev_info(eth->dev,
+		 "AN7563 dbg: dev_open dev=%s gdm_id=%u pse_port=%u (no_npu=%d)\n",
+		 dev->name, port->id, pse_port, eth->soc->no_npu);
+
 #if defined(CONFIG_PCS_AIROHA)
 	if (airhoa_is_phy_external(port)) {
 		err = phylink_of_phy_connect(port->phylink, dev->dev.of_node, 0);
@@ -3564,6 +3577,7 @@ static const struct airoha_eth_soc_data
 	.num_xsi_rsts = ARRAY_SIZE(en7581_xsi_rsts_names),
 	.num_ppe = 1,
 	.ppe_skip_flush_sram = true,
+	.no_npu = true,
 	/*
 	 * AN7563 silicon shares the EN7581 frame-engine and source-port
 	 * encoding (verified against the GPL en7523.dtsi and Xiaomi
